  5pm\n\nLocation\n\nMonash College\, 750 Collins St\, Docklands VIC 3008\n
 \nOverview\n\nThe Economics of Mixed Systems short course introduces parti
 cipants to the economic principles underlying Australia's complex public-p
 rivate health care system. Topics include understanding the role of privat
 e health insurance\, consumer demand for public and private care\, waiting
  time dynamics\, supply-side factors such as physician dual practice and c
 ream-skimming\, and contemporary issues facing the sector.\n\nLearning out
 comes\n\nAt the end of the course\, participants will be able to:\n\nWho s
 hould attend?\n\nThe course is designed for those seeking to apply economi
 c concepts and evidence to current health policy issues. No prior economic
 s knowledge is required\; material is presented in a non-technical way wit
 h opportunities for group discussion.\n\nSuitable for:\n\nCost\n\nFees inc
 lude attendance at a full day of face-to-face seminars and group work\, ca
 tered lunch\, morning and afternoon tea.\n\nTeaching staff\n\nA/Prof Cheng
  is an expert on the economics of public and private health systems. He ha
 s published extensively in leading international journals on topics coveri
 ng public and private healthcare and insurance\, medical labour markets\, 
 international markets for healthcare\, and health and well-being. He is cu
 rrently on the editorial board of the international journal <em>Health Sys
 tems and Reform</em>.\n\nA/Prof Cheng has held academic and research appoi
 ntments at universities in Australia\, Singapore and the United States. He
  returned to Australia in 2024 after a three-year stint as a Research Scie
 ntist of Health Systems Research and Policy at the Harvard T.H. Chan Schoo
 l of Public Health. He has consulted for the World Health Organisation\, t
 he World Bank and various government departments in Australia.\n\nProgram\
 n\nEnrolments\n\n<a class="btn" href="https://events.humanitix.com/centre-
 for-health-economics-short-courses-26-and-27-may" target="_blank">Enrol no
 w</a>\n\nUpon successful completion of this course you will be awarded a M
 onash digital badge to share with your network.\n\nEnquiries\n\nFor enquir
 ies\, please email <a href="mailto:che_support@monash.edu">CHE Support</a
 >.
